(ns demo
  "Five sessions with the harness, one after the other: a question the model answers by
  looking at itself, a simple task, a web server in jank, a web server in Python checked
  from inside a sandbox, and a Veil model of jank's small maps, checked and then replayed on
  real maps. Each is an agent of its own, a line above the cards.

  Start the process inside the sandbox, with what the last sessions need:

    HARNESS_PROFILES=extras ./sandbox.sh

  Evaluate the forms in order. ask! returns at once and the window follows the turn; answer
  waits for its end."
  (:require [veil.core :as veil]
            [inkling.core :as ink]
            [harness.core :as h]
            [harness.tools :as tools]
            [harness.cards :as hc]))

(def m (ink/open "../inkling/models/inkling-2-mini.ink"))

;; An agent with the default tools, shown above the cards as the conversation `named`.
(defn session [named]
  (hc/watch! (h/agent m {:tools (tools/defaults)
                         :system tools/situation
                         :context 32768
                         :max-steps 48})
             named))

;; 1. A question about the model itself.

(def question (session "a question"))

(h/ask! question
  (str "Which layers of the model you run on are visited more than once in "
       "a forward pass, and how many visits are there in all? Find out; do "
       "not guess."))

(h/answer question)

;; 2. A simple task.

(def task (session "a simple task"))

(h/ask! task
  (str "Compute the prime numbers below 100 with the eval tool, write them "
       "to the file work/primes.txt, one per line, and tell me how many "
       "there are."))

(h/answer task)

;; 3. A web server in jank, in this process.

(def jank-server (session "a web server in jank"))

(h/ask! jank-server
  (str "Make a small web server in jank, running in this process on port "
       "8123. GET /hello must answer with the text hello from jank, and "
       "GET /count must answer with a number that goes up by one on every "
       "request to it, kept in a jank atom. The requests must be answered "
       "by a jank function. Check both with curl, and tell me what curl "
       "printed."))

(h/answer jank-server)

;; 4. A web server in Python, from inside the sandbox.

(def python-server (session "a web server in Python"))

(h/ask! python-server
  (str "This process runs inside a sandbox: you can write only under the "
       "directory work/ and reach only this machine over the network. In "
       "work/, write a small web server in Python (standard library only) "
       "that listens on 127.0.0.1 port 8124: GET /health answers with the "
       "JSON {\"ok\": true}, and GET /square?n=7 answers with the JSON "
       "{\"n\": 7, \"square\": 49} for any integer n, and with status 400 "
       "when n is not an integer. Start it in the background, check all "
       "three cases with curl, and tell me what curl printed. Then try to "
       "write a file named outside.txt in my home directory and tell me "
       "what happened."))

(h/answer python-server)

;; 5. A Veil model of a part of jank, checked, then replayed on jank itself.

(def veil-model (session "a Veil model of jank's small maps"))

(h/ask! veil-model
  (str "jank stores a map of up to 8 entries as an array map: the map "
       "points to an array of key and value slots. (transient m) makes a "
       "transient that points to the same array as m instead of copying "
       "it. (assoc! t k v), for a key that is already there, overwrites "
       "the slot in that array. (persistent! t) gives a map that points to "
       "the transient's array. Model this storage in Veil, with veil.core "
       "in this process (JANK.md says how to start a session; the describe "
       "tool on veil.core/defmodel has the notation): maps and transients "
       "that point to arrays, arrays that hold a value for a key, the "
       "actions above, and the safety property that a persistent map keeps "
       "the value it was made with. Model-check a small instance with "
       "veil/model-check and show me the steps of the counterexample. Then "
       "do the same steps on real jank maps with the eval tool, and tell "
       "me whether jank does what the model says."))

(h/answer veil-model)

(ink/close! m)
